{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:61c60740fc0a2fa6","name":"Braxus Lyn","source":{"id":"source:reference-61c60740fc0a2fa6","title":"Braxus Lyn","revision":22245,"timestamp":"2024-09-01T19:08:44Z","sha256":"04a45fec80077dd3fe744e48127dc0b289a7a47b45f699a96cb735084b093891","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=22245","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Braxus%20Lyn&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-61c60740fc0a2fa6","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Braxus Lyn is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clawdite"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clawdite","referenceId":"reference:b706bef304df2587"}," mercenary and general con artist for hire. Although she has seen her share of action during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", she is not technically a member of the Separatists' forces, preferring to remain a freelancer. Lyn specializes in fixing problems, particularly problems that involve intrigue and espionage.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["She was hired by the Separatists to help keep the wealthy elite of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tirahnn"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tirahnn","referenceId":"reference:c4cb12d6d6a545b7"}," under control, and she was tapped to rescue ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commander Zolghast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commander_Zolghast"}," when news of his capture reached the Separatists. Realizing that the Republic would have both troops and Probe Droids throughout the city, she disguised herself as Master ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ezar Elasra"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ezar_Elasra?action=edit&redlink=1"}," so that any Republic forces they encountered would be less likely to suspect deception. Gifted with basic ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Sensitivity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Sensitivity","referenceId":"reference:5202cab02f367bcf"}," and a few tricks she has picked up in her travels, she has managed to maintain the deception thus far.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Tactics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Since Lyn's mission is to get ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zolghast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zolghast","referenceId":"reference:a4a2d4cb45b05008"}," on the ship and to keep him alive, her first instinct when to heroes arrive is to maintain the bluff. She uses her ",{"tag":"a","children":["Deception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Deception","referenceId":"reference:17455029fb9994a3"}," skill to disguise herself as Master Elasra. Should the heroes see through the deception, she leaps into action, hurling enemies away with ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," (she will spend ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"}," to regain the use of ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Thrust"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Thrust","referenceId":"reference:71dad1bff9398936"}]}," when necessary) and generally moving enemies into a position where the ",{"tag":"a","children":["B1-Series Battle Droid Squads"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/B1-Series_Battle_Droid_Squads"}," have optimal shots.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Braxus Lyn Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clawdite"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clawdit